---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<Base title="VoltUI runtime and usage" titleEn="VoltUI runtime and usage" titleZh="VoltUI 运行时与用量" description="Understand the local runtime state and evidence boundaries for VoltUI.">
  <SiteHeader active="usage" />
  <main class="wrap"><section class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">RUNTIME / 运行时</div><h1>Inspect the same local runtime contract you ship.</h1><p>VoltUI does not invent a parallel usage ledger or provider catalog. The official DSH profile owns session and tool state; Electron reports lifecycle failures and package identity at the shell boundary.</p></section><section class="home-section"><div class="grid"><article class="feat"><div class="n">01</div><h3>Runtime identity</h3><p>Record the exact DSH package, Node version, profile patch and commit SHA used for a build.</p><code>@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.1-rc.2</code></article><article class="feat"><div class="n">02</div><h3>Process health</h3><p>The shell waits for a trusted loopback URL and reclaims the child process on exit.</p><code>dsh web: http://127.0.0.1:&lt;port&gt;</code></article><article class="feat"><div class="n">03</div><h3>Workspace scope</h3><p>DSH starts in the canonical workspace selected by the launch environment.</p><code>DSH_WORKSPACE</code></article><article class="feat"><div class="n">04</div><h3>Credential scope</h3><p>Provider secrets remain in the official runtime's credential/settings surface, never in the Electron renderer.</p><code>DSH_HOME</code></article></div></section><section class="band"><h2>Evidence over promises.</h2><p>Use the repository checks and the generated Windows artifact hash as the release record.</p><a class="btn btn-dark" href="https://github.com/zuohuadong/volt-gui/actions">View CI</a></section></main><SiteFooter />
</Base>
